To find the total number of thorns, we multiply the number of rose bushes by the number of roses per bush, and then multiply by the number of thorns per rose:

$$
3 \text{ rose bushes} \times 25 \text{ roses per bush} = 75 \text{ roses}
$$
$$
75 \text{ roses} \times 8 \text{ thorns per rose} = 600 \text{ thorns}
$$

$$
\boxed{600}
$$
